+### Retry a failed step
+
+When a step fails, the page keeps the completed steps and offers **Retry step**
+or **Stop**. Retry repeats that step, then continues. The downloaded IPA and
+Apple session stay available; an install retry reuses the signed app and opens
+a fresh tunnel. A handover retry only sends the pairing file again, without
+reinstalling. Cancelled prompts and sign-ins stop without offering a retry.
+In the terminal the same choice is **Retry this step?**.
+
+### Install a local IPA
+
+The page first offers **Download SideInstaller**, or a file picker for an
+`.ipa` already in Files. Pick it and tap **Use selected IPA**. The file is copied
+into Minis in small chunks and checked before the run continues. A failed
+import leaves the picker open to try again. Local files skip the GitHub check
+and release download; signing still needs Apple's servers, an Apple Account
+and LocalDevVPN. The uploaded copy is removed when the run ends.
+
+In the terminal, choose **Install a local IPA** and enter its path inside
+Minis, or pass it directly (quote paths containing spaces):
+
+```sh
+siboot --ipa "/path/to/My App.ipa"
+```
+
+The original file is left alone. Any app can be signed and installed this
+way; only SideInstaller receives SideInstaller's pairing-file handover and
+the **Open SideInstaller** button.
+
+These changes require a newly built siboot binary. The `bin/siboot-aarch64`
+already in this checkout and the upstream install command still run the
+published build; see [Building](#building) to rebuild and update its checksum.
+
